<title>INDIA: TABLE - India's ITC Classic slips into red.</title>
<headline>TABLE - India's ITC Classic slips into red.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net Profit (loss)   (2,849.94) vs  313.41</p>
<p>    Net sales		1,761.72 vs 3,109.25</p>
<p>    Other income	  14.60  vs    12.01</p>
<p>    Total expenditure  571.71  vs   374.88</p>
<p>    Interest costs   1,852.52  vs 1,742.38</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 410.12  vs   552.07</p>
<p>NOTE: ITC Classic Finance Ltd, an affiliate of ITC Ltd, said in a statement its results were adversely affected by a liquidity crunch hurting the company's corporate clients and unprecedented premature withdrawals of the company's fixed deposits between October 1996 and January 1997.</p>
<p>--  New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
